WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.150
- I realize that success is fleeting.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.730
As a fighter, you're only as good

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.580
as your last fight because
as soon as you win,

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.130
the clock starts ticking again.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.810
That's what drives me to evolve

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.685
and improve every day
in everything that I do.

00:00:16.685 --> 00:00:19.268
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.470
My name is May Ooi.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.010
- [Narrator] May has mastered more things

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.070
than most will in a lifetime.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.670
Her path to greatness started back

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.910
when she took up swimming as a child.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.700
May would go on to compete
in the 1992 Olympics

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.213
in Barcelona, representing Singapore.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.550
- I was swimming competitively

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.810
for about 14 years, and at the end of that

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.760
I was just really tired
of the training regimen,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:53.760
the pressure from competition,
and not having a normal life.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:54.910
- [Narrator] She went to college

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.760
and eventually medical
school, but then she stumbled

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.593
on a martial art called capoeira,

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:04.320
fell in love with it and
she mastered that, too.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.973
That was her first step into MMA.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.880
- MMA means mixed martial arts.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.060
You will be fighting against an opponent

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.480
in the cage but you can use any form

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.440
of martial arts that
you're comfortable with.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.130
I started with capoeira.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.760
I have really good ground game in jujitsu,

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.620
so I like to take my fights to the floor,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.570
and I like to finish my
opponents on the floor.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:30.610
I think I've choked out
most of my opponents.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:33.380
When I was training,
recreationally, I got really good

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.330
and a lot of people asked me to compete.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:37.120
I refused to because I didn't want to be

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.710
in that competitive environment anymore.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:43.060
But I met Harlow Gracie, who is royalty

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.610
in the martial arts world.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.250
- [Narrator] Once he saw May train he knew

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.350
that she was destined for greatness.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.880
He encouraged her to compete,
and so she did for five years,

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.353
becoming one of Singapore's best fighters.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.280
And now May is taking time
away from competition,

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.700
and once again, mastering something new.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.070
- We're gonna work on the jinga first.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:12.553
I work with children from
two and a half to 12.

00:02:12.553 --> 00:02:15.110
(calling out fighting terms)

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.350
I grew up in a middle-class family,

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.850
and I didn't have a lot of opportunities.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:24.850
But through swimming and sports
I had amazing opportunities,

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.950
and I had a lot of doors
that opened for me.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:31.910
Now that I have the means to
give back I like to give back

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.080
to Singapore and help grow

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.780
the sporting culture in Singapore.

00:02:36.629 --> 00:02:39.046
(calm music)

